// Every token type the scanner can produce, once, plus the inputs most likely to
// be lexed wrong. Its dump is pinned in clox/test/expected-tokens.txt.

( ) { } , . - + ; / *
! != = == > >= < <=

and class else false for fun if nil or print return super this true var while

// Keyword prefixes and extensions. `orchid` is the one that breaks a scanner
// that matches keywords against the input instead of scanning a maximal run
// first: it lexes as `or` followed by `chid`.
orchid format further andy classy printer
a c e f i n o p r s t v w fa fo fu th tr

foo _bar baz123 A_1 _

0 123 123.456

// A dot with no digit after it is not part of the number, which is what makes
// `123.sqrt()` parse. A dot with no digit before it is not part of one either.
123.sqrt
.5

"" "hello" "a b c" "keywords like and or if are text in here"

"line one
line two"

// Challenge 1. The first is the book's own example; the second is its nesting
// question; the third has an ordinary block inside the interpolation, which is
// the case the brace counter exists for.
"${drink} will be ready in ${steep + cool} minutes."
"Nested ${"interpolation?! Are you ${"mad?!"}"}"
"${ {} }"

// An error is a token and scanning continues past it, so the identifier after
// these two is still found.
@ # keepgoing

// A comment is whitespace, so this line produces nothing at all.
"unterminated
